    "findings": [
      "ShaderInfoBuilder keeps EnableAsyncCompile tied to the gameplay async setting even when fromCache=true.",
      "VulkanRenderer forwards this flag to ShaderCollection. With async=false and a pipeline state, its constructor launches BackgroundCompilation and returns before assigning the detached warm-up flag.",
      "That non-background branch waits for shader modules and then creates an initial compute/graphics pipeline. CheckProgramLink waits for its task; the cache loader calls blocking validation.",
      "The existing detached-warm-up branch only applies to compileInBackground=true.",
      "InitializeShaderCache sets the GPU-ready event only after all physical-memory shader caches initialize; ArmProcessContext.Execute waits for that event before guest execution."
    ],
    "hypothesis": "This source path explains why startup may still spend time creating initial pipelines while gameplay async shaders is false. The repeated warnings are compatible with this work; their count and timing do not quantify the CPU cost of logging or prove failed pipelines.",
    "not_claimed": [
      "The log identifies the reviewed engine build.",
      "All 2743 cached programs produced new Metal compilations.",
      "Each warning corresponds to a failed pipeline.",
      "Enabling gameplay async shaders is required or validated as a fix.",
      "A new startup optimization has been measured on the device."
    ]
